[{:db/id 17592186162056 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5de95c02-fd0e-5b80-9aec-f79ce1a6a7f4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5de95c02-fd0e-5b80-9aec-f79ce1a6a7f4" :question/id #uuid "5de95c02-fd0e-5b80-9aec-f79ce1a6a7f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-109040" :question/problem "$\\text{Var}[4]=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[a]=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[4]=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a48e8e98-7e33-5d3a-b817-98548380f899"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a48e8e98-7e33-5d3a-b817-98548380f899" :answer-field/id #uuid "a48e8e98-7e33-5d3a-b817-98548380f899" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d97479d6-3612-564b-bc2b-b05d469953d6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d97479d6-3612-564b-bc2b-b05d469953d6" "answer-01e8d53a-c37d-54b9-846a-15a7e518c2f5" "answer-d253879a-8d9a-5864-96bf-478e85b5c3b6" "answer-b143f08b-1cca-5921-99e5-5bc87f00cffc" "answer-60665ee3-a83d-5432-a05d-60a88ce923d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d97479d6-3612-564b-bc2b-b05d469953d6" :answer/id #uuid "d97479d6-3612-564b-bc2b-b05d469953d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01e8d53a-c37d-54b9-846a-15a7e518c2f5" :answer/id #uuid "01e8d53a-c37d-54b9-846a-15a7e518c2f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d253879a-8d9a-5864-96bf-478e85b5c3b6" :answer/id #uuid "d253879a-8d9a-5864-96bf-478e85b5c3b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b143f08b-1cca-5921-99e5-5bc87f00cffc" :answer/id #uuid "b143f08b-1cca-5921-99e5-5bc87f00cffc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60665ee3-a83d-5432-a05d-60a88ce923d1" :answer/id #uuid "60665ee3-a83d-5432-a05d-60a88ce923d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162057 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eff26da6-299d-5b1f-93b8-02b4dbf809cb" "question-ab459c95-a786-5463-b6df-ba7f08de2795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-eff26da6-299d-5b1f-93b8-02b4dbf809cb" :question/id #uuid "eff26da6-299d-5b1f-93b8-02b4dbf809cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109064" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=3,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[7X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X] & ={7}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =49\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=3.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}+4\\cdot \\frac{2}{7}+16\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{73}{7}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[7X] & =49\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =49\\cdot \\frac{10}{7} \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cee9d609-cf3a-562f-9f5d-2dd12fbb70da"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cee9d609-cf3a-562f-9f5d-2dd12fbb70da" :answer-field/id #uuid "cee9d609-cf3a-562f-9f5d-2dd12fbb70da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a997e5ce-81f8-5baf-8303-e27befaf4b42" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd1bccd5-410f-5b91-93ca-dbe4d676607f" "answer-a997e5ce-81f8-5baf-8303-e27befaf4b42" "answer-1cce534e-4802-5d94-97bf-80beed889e95" "answer-e6c7e480-2dae-55a9-9956-216be43bcfc5" "answer-f5361e88-3d20-5f4f-860f-c82dceb66009"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd1bccd5-410f-5b91-93ca-dbe4d676607f" :answer/id #uuid "bd1bccd5-410f-5b91-93ca-dbe4d676607f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a997e5ce-81f8-5baf-8303-e27befaf4b42" :answer/id #uuid "a997e5ce-81f8-5baf-8303-e27befaf4b42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1cce534e-4802-5d94-97bf-80beed889e95" :answer/id #uuid "1cce534e-4802-5d94-97bf-80beed889e95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "73" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6c7e480-2dae-55a9-9956-216be43bcfc5" :answer/id #uuid "e6c7e480-2dae-55a9-9956-216be43bcfc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{49}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5361e88-3d20-5f4f-860f-c82dceb66009" :answer/id #uuid "f5361e88-3d20-5f4f-860f-c82dceb66009" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ab459c95-a786-5463-b6df-ba7f08de2795" :question/id #uuid "ab459c95-a786-5463-b6df-ba7f08de2795" :question/math-academy-id "q-109070" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{9}{2},$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X] & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{9}{2}.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+36\\cdot \\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{2}X] & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-49d01f52-f12f-5f40-8306-2b10fa6ebffd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-49d01f52-f12f-5f40-8306-2b10fa6ebffd" :answer-field/id #uuid "49d01f52-f12f-5f40-8306-2b10fa6ebffd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8456a043-c86f-5008-9d67-2741aff12dc5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7efbea4c-7fba-5238-8596-49239d557793" "answer-e9634791-3b57-5087-836f-34d41f943f0e" "answer-771854e8-d892-5203-a97d-09439ca5fe0b" "answer-b334ddce-463a-5f5a-8086-6f71f3ca1947" "answer-8456a043-c86f-5008-9d67-2741aff12dc5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer